WEBVTT

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Hello, I'm Bob Ross, and I'd like to welcome you

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.920
to the 10th Joy of Painting series.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:35.850
If this is your first time with us,

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.670
I hope you grab a few paints and some brushes

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:38.990
and come along and paint with us.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:41.030
If you've been with us before, first of all,

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:43.070
I'd like to thank you for inviting me back again.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.320
So I tell you what, let's have them graphically

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.740
run all the colors across the screen

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.760
that you need to do this painting with me,

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.320
and they'll come across in the same order

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.880
that I have on the palette, starting with a titanium white

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.160
and working all the way around.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.340
While they're doing that, let's go on up here

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.060
and talk a second.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.860
This is an 18 by 24 canvas.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.300
This is a double-primed, pre-stretched canvas.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.720
And I've covered it with a nice, thin, even coat

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.020
of the liquid white, which makes it wet, makes it slick.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.160
It allows us to actually blend color right here on the canvas.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.640
So we have that ready, so let's get together

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.160
and let's do a fantastic painting.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.680
I'm gonna start off today with a small amount of phthalo blue.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:21.200
And we'll just take and pull a little bit out,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.420
and then tap the brush.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.800
That assures a nice, even distribution of color

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:26.920
all the way through the brush.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:29.350
Just tap it, just tap, like so.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:29.880
Yes.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.420
Let's go right up here.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.810
Now then, let's start right up in here

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:34.850
and we'll use little criss-cross strokes.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.190
Just make little X's,

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.450
and let's put in a happy little cloud, little sky.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.090
Okay, a little more of the color.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.940
This thalo blue is very pretty, bright and shiny.

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:48.270
It's a happy color.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.380
Just continually use these little criss-cross strokes

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:54.420
and allow the color to,

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.260
it just literally blends with a liquid white.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.640
And as you work downward here,

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.990
and you get all these fantastic little effects

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:05.210
automatically, you see, isn't that easy?

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:09.630
That easy, you have a quick little sky, there.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.190
Now, while I have this on the brush,

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:15.860
tell you what, let's add the least little amount

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.190
of phthalo blue, or phthalo green, I mean.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:21.380
So we have phthalo blue and phthalo green,

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.300
just a small amount of the green, it's very strong.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:24.570
Let's go back up here.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.820
Maybe we'll have a little water in here,

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.280
so we'll just pull.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:33.360
right across like this, very gently.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:38.340
And pull from the outside in, there.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.410
Try to pull though from the outside in.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.990
If you start here and come across,

00:02:44.050 --> 00:02:45.190
it'll leave a great big mark.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.810
It's very hard to blend out.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.600
We want to make this as easy as possible.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.320
Here, all we'll do is just blend that together.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.680
And that little light area remains right here

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.390
and it sort of gives the illusion

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.860
of a silhouette of light coming across.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.190
there, just a little shiny area.

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.610
Okay, let's wash our brush now.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.580
If you've painted with me before,

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.100
you know this is the fun part.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.900
We wash our brushes with odorless thinner.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.770
Shake off the excess.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.390
Just beat the devil out of it.

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:20.370
All right, now with a nice clean brush,

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:21.550
now we'll go right back up here,

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.600
and we'll just blend the sky out a little bit.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.250
Still using the little criss-cross strokes.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.020
Now you can work this sky until it's absolutely dead

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.960
or you can leave some of these little dark

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.440
and light areas in it to give it some life.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:42.020
Very gently, we'll blend it to take out the brush strokes,

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:43.830
come right across the bottom,

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:45.920
and we have a happy little sky.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.730
That easy, that easy.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:57.390
Okay, now then, let's make some big fluffy clouds today.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:03:59.970
I'm gonna go right into the titanium water.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.000
with a one-inch brush.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.540
Pick up the least little touch of the bright red.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.780
Very small amount, it's very strong.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:08.860
Eat up your whole world.

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:11.980
Okay, load a lot of paint into the brush.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:12.680
Let's go up here now.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:14.940
Now maybe there's a happy little clouds

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.220
that just sort of float right around in the sky

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:17.820
and have fun.

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.670
Just sort of mix them up on here.

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:23.310
Clouds are very free.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.720
Just let them play, let them play.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.000
Maybe he comes right off in here

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:29.960
and goes off the top of the...

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:33.230
the canvas, wherever, wherever.

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:38.190
This is your world, so you create any kind of illusion

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.230
that you want in your world.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:42.350
There we go.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.170
And these are just little floaters, little happy clouds.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:51.650
And you can put as many or as few as you want.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:57.900
Now then, we'll take clean, dry, be sure it's dry,

00:04:58.760 --> 00:04:59.960
two inch brush, and I'm going to

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.770
We're gonna just gently blend it

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:04.450
using tiny little circular strokes,

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:08.990
tiniest little strokes, and just blend this together.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:13.300
Just blend it, just sort of mix it up.

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:22.050
Then we're gonna lift it, this sort of fluffs the cloud.

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:27.760
Just fluffs it right up, like so, see?

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:28.920
And then very lightly.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:32.810
There we go, isn't that fantastic?

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.720
You could do a happy little cloud that easy.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:40.260
Okay, shoot, we're just going right along here.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.520
Tell you what, I lived in Alaska,

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:46.470
oh gosh, nearly 14 years or so,

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:48.090
and I really like mountains,

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:49.650
so let's do a fantastic little mountain.

00:05:49.790 --> 00:05:52.250
I'm gonna take some black, some Prussian blue,

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:54.450
some Van Dyke brown,

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:57.350
we'll put some alizarin crimson in there too.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.960
Be careful with the crimson, or your mountain will-

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.170
turn purple, which is alright, that's alright.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:06.160
They wrote a beautiful song about purple mountains.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:09.470
Pull it out very flat and then cut across

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.810
so you have a small roll of paint

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:11.970
right out of the edge of the knife.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.490
There you go, go up here.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.790
Now then, you have to make an almighty decision.

00:06:16.890 --> 00:06:17.710
Where does your mountain live?

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:19.660
I think he's gonna live.

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:20.870
He is now.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:21.960
Right there.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.100
Maybe there's a bump there.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:29.890
You just sort of make a decision.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.270
and put it in.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:34.710
Mountain's growing, all kinds of shapes and colors,

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:40.160
and you're restricted only by your imagination.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:43.700
This right over like that.

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:46.610
Scrape off all the excess paint here.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:49.360
I'm just really using firm pressure,

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.920
pushing that paint right into the fabric.

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:58.130
I'll take a two inch brush, and I wanna grab it and pull.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:06:59.860
This removes excess.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:02.590
paint and blends it out so it gets lighter at the bottom.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.970
You can see the entire mountain, it's always lighter

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.090
at the bottom than it is at the top,

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:12.630
because we have mist and pollution and all those things

00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:16.530
that break up and diffuse light, see?

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:19.020
Because this is wet, you can just move this paint,

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.080
you can pull it, you can move it all over the canvas.

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:25.890
This was a dry canvas, you'd be in agony city right now.

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.920
There we go, now let's go back to the night.

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:33.080
and let's put some snow on this mountain.

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:35.650
For that, I'll take the titanium white

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:37.710
and pull it out very flat,

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:42.140
and then cut across to get that little roll of paint again.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.070
See there? Okay, let's go back up here.

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.030
Now, think where your light's coming from.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:48.970
You have to start making some big decisions now.

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:51.670
If you're right-handed, normally it's easier for the light

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:52.810
to come from the right side.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.980
So let's go right here, touch, no pressure.

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:58.510
Just the weight of the knife, no pressure.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:07:59.810
See there?

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.120
Let it float right down the side of that mountain.

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.050
Look at there, look at there.

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:10.840
Follow the angles in your mountain and let it float.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:15.370
Absolutely no pressure, pressure.

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:18.260
Tend it, if you're not careful,

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:20.520
your hand will just literally float away.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:26.050
Just float away, very soft and very gentle.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.520
See, and then you have to make big decisions.

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:33.460
Maybe this peak right here, oh look here,

00:08:33.580 --> 00:08:34.380
look here, there it comes.

00:08:34.970 --> 00:08:38.430
See, you can bring it right in front.

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:40.040
You can move mountains.

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:42.440
You can do anything on this canvas.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.920
This canvas, you have total power.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:49.280
Absolutely.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:51.860
Now then, let's put some shadows in there.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:54.180
For that, I'm gonna take some white,

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.500
we'll put a little Prussian blue in it.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:59.180
Just white, Prussian blue.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.770
Mix it up to us about that color.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.850
Pull it out very flat again, cut across.

00:09:06.460 --> 00:09:08.080
Once again, we have a small roll of paint.

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:09.760
It's very important how you load this knife.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:10.880
Just go back up here.

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:15.190
Touch and just pull down.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:17.410
Now we're following the angles on the other side of the mill.

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.750
Watch here, I wanna push that back,

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:23.430
so I'll come from here and then I'll come distinctly through.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.010
See how it pushes that peak right back?

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:26.830
That's sneaky, huh?

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:29.960
Easy to do, you can do it.

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:33.030
You really can do it, there's no big secret here.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:34.510
We'll show you everything that you need

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:36.700
to paint fantastic paintings.

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.280
See, when you put those shadows in there,

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:45.200
everything just sort of pops out at you.

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:46.730
It brings it alive.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:49.060
The shadows are very important.

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:52.590
See, now we have a little hunk of paint right here

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:56.350
that doesn't look like much until we add a shadow under it.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:57.800
See there, you add a shadow,

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.380
and it becomes a separate entity.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:01.900
becomes a ridge all by itself.

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:03.260
Come right over in here,

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:09.120
just pull in all kinds of happy things,

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:12.610
and you can move these mountains

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:13.930
anywhere that you want them.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:14.860
Cheer.

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:18.800
Sometimes it's fun just to play some games.

00:10:19.240 --> 00:10:20.380
You can come right down in here,

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:25.390
and there, there's another peak.

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:29.760
That easy, easy.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.310
But when you put the shadow in here,

00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:36.190
then it really becomes a personality all on its own.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:39.940
You can create little ridges wherever you want them,

00:10:41.150 --> 00:10:42.750
and it's just a game of angles.

00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:44.790
Mountains are just geometric shapes.

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:50.250
You can take, maybe I'll bring this one

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:52.150
distinctly in front of that.

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:58.070
Pushes that mountain back.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:10:59.820
This is one of the ways that you create

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.400
depth and distance in your painting.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:05.420
There we go, just work with different planes.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:12.000
Okay, I get carried away sometimes.

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:13.360
I really like to paint mountains,

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:16.000
and I just, I'd cover up the whole canvas with mountains.

00:11:16.650 --> 00:11:18.010
And that's not bad when you're learning.

00:11:18.150 --> 00:11:20.010
Take an old canvas and start at the top

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:21.350
and paint all the way down with mountains,

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:23.940
and then just zip them right off and do it again.

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:25.060
That's the way you learn.

00:11:25.200 --> 00:11:27.420
If there's a secret to anything, it's practice.

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:29.390
Just practice.

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:31.420
and you really can do this.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:35.140
I get hundreds and hundreds of letters

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:37.160
from people all over the country,

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:39.380
just like you and I,

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:41.500
and they're painting beautiful pictures.

00:11:42.140 --> 00:11:44.690
Mm, some of the series we've showed,

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:46.450
some of the photographs that people have sent,

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:48.170
almost unbelievable.

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:52.270
All I'm doing is tapping and then lifting upward.

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:55.320
The lifting upward, like that, removes the tap marks

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:57.780
and creates that nice, soft, misty area down there.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:11:59.890
And over here,

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.020
we follow these angles.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.960
Always follow the angles that you've created

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:04.840
in your mountains, see there?

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:07.850
Ain't that easy, we got a happy mountain.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:15.880
Okay, let's make some little footy hills back here.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:18.880
I'm gonna start off and mix up some color.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.840
I'll just use this mountain color and let's put a little,

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:23.930
let's put some white with it and see what we have here.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.980
So that's just mainly some blue and black, alizarin.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.540
and crimson, and to that I'm gonna add

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:34.700
the least little touch, least little touch of sap green,

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:36.520
just to give it a little greenish color.

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:39.730
Part of it here I'm gonna add some white

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:43.060
and make it even lighter, just like so.

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:45.040
Okay, clean my knife.

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:48.880
Now then, let's use a different brush today.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:50.600
This is an oval brush.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:52.540
Maybe we can get a close-up shot of it.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:54.160
It's a little different, see?

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:55.020
It's sort of round.

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:57.840
This is an oval, a little different.

00:12:58.200 --> 00:12:58.900
Watch here, though.

00:12:59.640 --> 00:12:59.980
I'm gonna...

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.460
Fill it full of that color we just made.

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:04.960
Just really load it full of paint.

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:06.240
Okay, let's go right up here.

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:08.640
Now then, you have to make a big decision.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:11.190
Let's say a little footy hill lives right here,

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:12.570
and all I'm doing is just tapping.

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:14.260
Isn't that fantastic?

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:17.090
Look at all the little things it makes in there.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.520
Looks like just the tops of thousands of little trees

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:21.580
far off in the distance.

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:29.970
Isn't that a...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.860
Super easy way to make little footy hills.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:34.360
Now with a clean dry brush,

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:36.480
I wanna create some mist at the base of this.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:39.620
So what I'm gonna do is just tap the base.

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:41.900
Just the base down here, don't tap the top.

